2026-09-01T16:55Z claude note SCOPE CORRECTED by the raid on 0565/0566: Action 1 said "chunk worker over stored text", which is a survival of the three-process design SPEC §5.2.5 collapsed. The spec is explicit that "the boundary between chunk and embed survives as a **write ordering** rather than a process boundary: the conductor segments, and an item's slabs, entries and passages are durable before any vector for it is computed", and that a body-text embed order "carries an entry-sized range — the slab addresses §5.2.2 gives every passage — which the worker reads back read-only, slices, embeds and streams home". So passage cutting belongs to the conductor's segmentation loop (0565) and never to a chunk stage here; what this tranche owns of the body path is the ORDER — a range over text 0565 already stored — plus the embed worker, the quantum autotune and the sidecar. Action 1 rewritten accordingly; the title's "chunk" is left alone since ticket IDs and filenames are not renamed. This also settles 0565's own open question in the same direction, recorded there. Nothing else in this ticket changes: Actions 2-4 were always the embed side.
